    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6adbd476_f83b28bb",
        "filename": "src/core/SkScaleToSides.h",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 4623515
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-02T15:30:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Setting `*b \u003d maxCoord - minCoord` is not sufficient because floating-point subtraction is not exact when minCoord is much smaller than maxCoord or when `maxCoord - minCoord` rounds up.\n\n\n------\nfor example, `minCoord \u003d 1e-30f` and `maxCoord \u003d 100.0f`, `minCoord` is smaller than half an ULP of `maxCoord` (`ulp(100.0f) \u003d 7.63e-6`). \n\nAs a result, `maxCoord - minCoord` loses precision and evaluates to `100.0f`.\n\nBecause `100.0f - 1e-30f \u003d\u003d 100.0f`, setting `*b \u003d maxCoord - minCoord` leaves `*b \u003d 100.0f`.\n\nIn `are_radii_predicates_valid`, `ptFromMax \u003d maxCoord - *b \u003d 100.0f - 100.0f \u003d 0.0f`, so the validity check `minCoord \u003c\u003d ptFromMax` evaluates to `false` (`1e-30f \u003c\u003d 0.0f`)\n\nFor `maxCoord - *b \u003e\u003d minCoord` to be true, `*b` must be stepped down by 1 ULP to `nextafterf(100.0f, 0.0f)`\n\n----\n\n\nI repaced the while loop with a simpler `if (maxCoord - *b \u003c minCoord)` block. This does the same thing to guanrantee that `*b \u003c (maxCoord - minCoord)` and passes all the tests as well\n\n\nif `*b` is much greater than `(maxCoord - minCoord)`, we can just step it down to one ULP below `(maxCoord - minCoord)`",
      "parentUuid": "c2d412cb_13b6e659",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 0,
